## Biographies
Prof. Ying-Feng Han was born in 1980 in Shandong, China. He obtained his Ph.D. in chemistry at Fudan University in 2009 (supervisor Prof. Guo-Xin Jin). He is currently an Associate Professor in the Department of Chemistry at Fudan University. His research interests are primarily in the area of molecular architectures via selfassembly and carbene chemistry.
Prof. Guo-Xin Jin received his Ph.D. from Nanjing University in 1987. After postdoctoral work at the University of Bayreuth, Germany, he joined Changchun Institute of Applied Chemistry, Chinese Academy of Sciences, in 1996 as a professor. In 2001, he moved to Shanghai and held the position of Chair Professor (Cheung Kong Scholarship) of Inorganic Chemistry at Fudan University. His research interests are in organometallic chemistry, particularly in organometallic macrocyclic architecture and catalysts for olefin polymerization.
